# Multi-request session tracking

When the user asks for **multiple things**, or work spans **>1 subsystem / >1 agent turn**, create and maintain:

```
.local/sessions/YYYY-MM-DD_<shortId>_<slug>/
  REQUESTS.md  TODOS.md  PLAN.md  MEMORY.md  STATUS.md
```

- Copy starters from `.agents/templates/session/`.
- Full convention: `.agents/templates/session/README.md` and `.agents/execute/partials/session-tracking.md`.
- `.local/` is gitignored — never commit secrets.
- Keep `TODOS.md` / `STATUS.md` current; before handover every todo is `[x]` or deferred with a reason in `STATUS.md`.
- Follow-up messages that add more work **append** to the end of `TODOS.md` without being asked. Resume the interrupted task. Keep FIFO. Do not jump to the newest item. Quality gates wait until they stop adding items — `.cursor/rules/follow-up-burst.mdc`.
- Fabro stage artifacts (`PLAN.md` at module root, `.local/findings/scope.md`) stay as today — the session folder tracks **ad-hoc multi-request work** across Cursor / Claude / Fabro.
- Throwaway recon only: `.local/tmp/{id}/`. Gate backlog: `.local/quality-backlog.md`.

**Skip** for single-file / single-bug one-shots.
